                                "sense_id": "b4b22c00-e33b-3e8d-8718-27b5c215f915",
                                "text": "This is the Ideal, or Eidolon of worthship (value or trustworthiness) which is of sufficient causality to sustain the superstructures of science and philosophy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5c61127-bf4d-4184-98ec-488cff772793",
                                "sense_id": "b4b22c00-e33b-3e8d-8718-27b5c215f915",
                                "text": "2010, Carlton Pearson, God Is Not a Christian, Nor a Jew, Muslim, Hindu...\nYou know your \"worthship.\" The traditional church is afraid to allow you to discover it because you may lose your codependency on it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a16d9248-d8b0-4d57-b842-8cc26714f2ef",
                                "sense_id": "b4b22c00-e33b-3e8d-8718-27b5c215f915",
                                "text": "2020, Geoffrey Hindley, Medieval Siege and Siegecraft\n[…] a time when 'worthship', the respect considered owing to a merchant or guildsman, depended as much on physical wealth as on rank in the town hierarchy […]"
